(7705992, 1264919, 67258, '<td valign="top">I have come back to this so many times this week, and now I must decide on my vote.  I find myself completely torn - I do rather like this illustration effect that you have achieved - everything about it implies and suggests a coloured sketch - and in an extended editing challenge I would probably vote  highly.   I must assume that all your steps are standard editing legal, but part of me feels the the image has moved so far away from photography and into the realm of digital art that it is no longer a photograph.  

<br/>In this instance I am going to vote highly - I would love to be able to achieve this myself -  but at the same time, I would hate it if such heavily manipulated images  became the norm, crowding out more traditional takes on photography.  So, a one time only vote of 8, for showing me something new that I can aspire towards in my editing, but probably not for DPC.</td>', 'I have come back to this so many times this week, and now I must decide on my vote.  I find myself completely torn - I do rather like this illustration effect that you have achieved - everything about it implies and suggests a coloured sketch - and in an extended editing challenge I would probably vote  highly.   I must assume that all your steps are standard editing legal, but part of me feels the the image has moved so far away from photography and into the realm of digital art that it is no longer a photograph.  

In this instance I am going to vote highly - I would love to be able to achieve this myself -  but at the same time, I would hate it if such heavily manipulated images  became the norm, crowding out more traditional takes on photography.  So, a one time only vote of 8, for showing me something new that I can aspire towards in my editing, but probably not for DPC.', '2021-11-07 16:06:35.000000', NULL, 1),
